epiora-mdb test data provenance
===============================

testV1997.mdb, testIndexCodesV1997.mdb
    From jackcess (Apache-2.0), commit
    be0a2139b087a227d14cafd4ea231306a5a3a862 — the same pin the
    mdb-wasm spike used for testV1997.mdb. Upstream paths:
    src/test/data/V1997/{testV1997,testIndexCodesV1997}.mdb
      testV1997.mdb          SHA-256 27788b47e17412427830e80c2cb69366885aa11b12c61422de73029194bef135
      testIndexCodesV1997.mdb SHA-256 75c7b039f339e0cf364320ee988002811fd6c4e37e91033356fd16c7eb6a82b1
    testIndexCodesV1997.mdb (JET3, cp1252) is the code-page oracle:
    its Table1 `data` column holds "AA<byte>AA"-style cells covering
    the high half of cp1252, including the five bytes the page leaves
    undefined (0x81/0x8D/0x8F/0x90/0x9D stored raw).
    https://github.com/jahlborn/jackcess (Apache-2.0)

pwd-set.mdb
    From jackcessencrypt (Apache-2.0), commit
    e84161170c9b2811636ec32e039492241836705d, src/test/data/pwd-set.mdb.
    JET4 database with the database password "testpassword"; used by
    password_protected_is_typed.
    SHA-256 9177af1f5c01c66a3d3be9b61a975856285c18ce6f481baa158bf176726519a5
    https://github.com/jahlborn/jackcessencrypt (Apache-2.0)

Oswego12.native.csv
    `mdb-export` of the Oswego12 table, produced by the mdb-wasm
    spike's native mdbtools build (docs/spikes/mdb-wasm.md).
    SHA-256 ada2049737fcb31412692a979b1017ce11583a4c03d41d66b2b1ea7113d5de67

batches/sample/*.eptb
    Native-encoder oracle batches, one whole-table EPTB v1 batch per
    user table of fixtures/legacy/samples/ei7/Sample/Sample.mdb
    (SHA-256 c3f70af4aef2de572aadeb127e74661667642b325d9f0f2792f1e60e00f9078e).
    Regenerate: cargo run -p epiora-mdb --bin dump-batches -- \
      fixtures/legacy/samples/ei7/Sample/Sample.mdb \
      crates/epiora-mdb/tests/data/batches/sample
    The app parity test (app/src/legacy/mdb.test.ts) requires the
    committed wasm module to produce byte-identical batches.

batches/chunk7/*.eptb
    Native-encoder oracle chunks of the Oswego12 table, 7 rows per
    batch (`{name}.{row_offset}.eptb`). The app parity test requires
    `mdb.batches("Oswego12", 7)` from the committed wasm module to be
    byte-identical to them.
    Regenerate: cargo run -p epiora-mdb --bin dump-batches -- \
      fixtures/legacy/samples/ei7/Sample/Sample.mdb \
      crates/epiora-mdb/tests/data/batches/chunk7 \
      --table Oswego12 --chunk 7
